{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e","id":1339029,"title":"Adventure! 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-02T11:36:57-07:00","id":1339029,"title":"Adventure! 2e","content":"I definitely can imagine the way Stalwarts would work with Superior-esque rules. Add a Inspiration rating to allow them to overclock themselves (in the best Maxing Out rules, effect that was blocked from superiors to give no chance of gaining taint). Maybe limit the number of dots a Stalwart have in their powers to \u00bd Inspiration or to a facet (less probable)<br /> <br /> For Mesmerists I would keep the same idea as Psiads, but exchange Psi for Inspiration and limit all the modes. Probably make the base powers buyable by themselves and make the 1 and 2 dots available for theirs that have enough inspiration. Limit the Attunement Range and other effects to a lower level comparing to Psiad, possibly 1 Psi equal to 3 Inspiration. That means I would make a Superior Power stile for mesmerists, using the lower dots of the modes as reference.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Any different approach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T12:50:37-07:00","id":1339044,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think Mesmerists will have Modes. Ala 1e, they\u2019ll have a genre appropriate power list. We see a hint of this in the Psiad chapter of the Aexpansion, where it references how S.K. was the only of her kind with the Qk inherent powers, though some individuals had weaker versions of the same effects, but over time the Qk inherent powers became universal - it\u2019s talking about the transition from Mesmerists to Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T13:00:12-07:00","id":1339047,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of Mesmerists having Modes. <br /> <br /> That said, yeah I see a lot of potentials in how Supwriors work to how the inspired do. Like dot powers and prerequisites and such.<br /> <br /> I hope that basic powers juat work but that its only the advanced powers that need points to be spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T13:01:41-07:00","id":1339048,"title":"","content":"I would not make modes per se, but maybe use the idea of Forte from Superiors, dividing in Biological, Cognitive and Physical Powers with some Powers related to those themes coming from the first few dots. A 5dot power would be close to a 3 dots mode, but not all of them would be this powerful, most would range from 1dot to 3 dots, like superior powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:14:07-07:00","id":1339084,"title":"","content":"How I'd like to see TC:A! do things:<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd like to see three kinds of Inspired using one set of rules, which at the very least uses the Talents in TC as a starting point. The most minimal approach would be that Mesmerists, Stalwarts, and Daredevils are all Inspired, differing from each other only in the kinds of Gifts they get: Daredevils get Luck Gifts and Aptitude Gifts; Stalwarts get Dynamic Gifts; and Mesmerists get Psychic Gifts. There <i>could</i> be some further differentiation between the three types; but if so, it should be fairly minor. I'll get into some possibilities for each later in in this post. <br /> <br /> <u>Mesmerists</u><br /> I'm all for the idea of Mesmerists getting Psychic Gifts that are grouped into categories along the same lines as Modes, or at least Aptitudes. I'm also OK with the idea that a given Mesmerist might favor one or two of those categories over the others; but I'm also OK if they don't. I <i>don't</i> think the specific lists of Psychic Gifts needs to conform to the specific powers granted by Modes in TC:\u00c6. <br /> <br /> If Mesmerists have something unique to them, Is like it to be the synergy between different Aptitudes (along the lines of Combining Powers and Combining With Other Psions Or Psiads, \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion p.88). And if such a capability is introduced, I wouldn't mind seeing it benefit from the Reflective Facet in some way: not anything too major, as I wouldn't want to make the Reflective Facet become something that all Mesmerists must have; but of the three Facets, the Reflective Facet does seem to be the most in tune with how mesmerists operate. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't consider this to be a reasonable alternative to having access to Dramatic Editing: Mesmerists ought to be able to engage in Dramatic Editing, too, though they should perhaps have a less effective version of it (see below for more on this). And again, I'd be perfectly fine if mesmerists <i>don't</i> have a unique benefit that daredevils and stalwarts lack. In fact, given that psiads aren't as good at combining their powers as psions are, I think that it would be perfectly appropriate if mesmerists were even less capable in that regard, possibly to the extent that they have no appreciable synergistic benefits. (Reminder: synergy referred to combining several things in a way where the whole is greater than the sum of its parts.)<br /> <br /> <u>Stalwarts</u><br /> I could see Dynamic Gifts working like Superior powers from \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion, with stalwarts differing from Superiors only in that they have Inspiration on top of their Dynamic Gifts. That, and the lists of Dynamic Gifts don't necessarily have to match up one-to-one with Superior powers. But the general idea behind Superior powers (that is, they're inverse focused, centered on enhancing the character's innate capabilities rather than influencing the world around the character) works perfectly for Dynamic Gifts as well. <br /> <br /> If stalwarts get some sort of special ability, overclocking their Gifts would be appropriate. If something like this is included, If be inclined to somehow tie it to the Destructive Facet \u2014 but like my suggestion of tying a mesmerist's synergy to the Reflective Facet, this should be a minor influence that doesn't demand that all stalwarts invest in the Destructive Facet: there are thematic links between stalwarts and what the Destructive Facet represents (Intention over Luck or Skill), but these shouldn't be taken to a level that designing a stalwart without a Destructive Facet is a dumb move. <br /> <br /> Conversely, there are reasons why stalwarts probably <i>shouldn't</i> have overclocking: in TC:Ab, overclocking is innately tied to Quantum Flux and Transcendence \u2014 the tendency of a Nova to mutate into something that's arguably inhuman. This is <i>not</i> part of the stalwart experience; so if overclocking isn't included in TC:A!'s stalwarts, I won't mind.<br /> <br /> And as with the suggested mesmerist special ability, I don't see overclocking as a reasonable alternative to Dramatic Editing. Again, more on this below. <br /> <br /> <u>Daredevils</u><br /> Daredevils are almost entirely covered by the Talent rules found in TC. I'd give them a third category of Gifts that corresponds to the Destructive Facet and Intention the same way that Luck Gifts correspond to the Intuitive Facet and Luck and the way that Aptitude Gifts correspond to the Reflective Facet and Skill. That said, that \u201cthird category\u201d might merely be a case of splitting the Aptitude Gifts in TC into two, with skill-based Aptitude Gifts staying where they are and the attribute-based ones getting recategorized into the new Intention-themed category. <br /> <br /> If mesmerists and stalwarts get special capabilities, then the daredevils should have a special affinity with Dramatic Editing. It doesn't mean that they should have <i>exclusive</i> access to it; Dramatic Editing represents a genre convention that's part and parcel of the pulp adventures that TC:A! was inspired by, and the equivalent of stalwarts and mesmerists in the source material definitely had their share of convenient coincidences. But I could see daredevils being <i>better at it</i> than everyone else. I see two possibilities here: <br /> <br /> 1. Everyone in the game (including daredevils) can access Dramatic Editing through the use of Momentum, but daredevils are the only ones who can access it using Inspiration. Some thought would need to be put into what the Momentum costs for Dramatic Editing should be like, and/or to what extent Momentum-based Dramatic Editing can make changes: Momentum-based edits might cost twice as much Momentum as it would cost Inspiration, and/or you might not even be allowed to conduct the third or even the second level of Dramatic Editing through Momentum. <br /> <br /> 2. All of the Inspired have access to the Dramatic Editing rules found in TC, but Daredevils have access to a superior version. This is one of the few ideas from the Trinity Universe d20 books that I liked: Improved Dramatic Editing, where a given character could get a discount on a particular class of Dramatic Edits based on his, well, class. In TC:A!, this would translate to your Origin and/or Role Path being used to justify a possible price break on Dramatic Editing: if you can justify a particular Edit as resonating with your Path, you can roll your Intuitive Facet to reduce the cost of the Edit by one. This <i>can</i> make it free. <br /> <br /> That said, I'd also be perfectly fine with daredevils working exactly like Talents do in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:23:11-07:00","id":1339085,"title":"","content":"It jumps out to me that there are two strong contenders on how to do Mesmerists and Stalwarts. Possibility 1 is to use the example of Superiors and don\u2019t give them a power or fuel stat, balancing the powers they can buy accordingly. This plays up how for the Stalwarts and Mesmerists, there is no growth beyond this state (at least without another transformative empowering evolutionary jump). Future individuals may activate as Psiads and Novas with room to expand in power, but for these individuals, their nature and tier is static.<br /> <br /> The second option is to treat them as divergent evolution from Talents that later evolve into completely separate things. They use the same mechanical framework as Talents with Facets and Inspiration, but just have different Gifts.<br /> <br /> The latter option will mean weaker purchasable powers than the first option, but access to Dramatic Editing, and play up how evolution isn\u2019t a straight line from weaker to stronger, but a branching path of divergent adaptations from common ancestry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-02-2019, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T18:16:47-07:00","id":1339094,"title":"","content":"I think Mesmerists will have simplified powers compared to Psiads and Modes. It could be interesting if they were like what you would get if you mixed a Psiad with a Talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T18:32:26-07:00","id":1339095,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think they will make Mesmerists and Stalwarts without Inspiration rating, but the lacking for Superiors also surprised me.<br /> The approach from what are Stalwarts and Mesmerists is really complex, and there were several main discussions about it before.<br /> <br /> If you put them as Talents that are evolving to Novas and Psiads, or at least a point in between them, than you have access to DE for all, but at same time, the entire idea of Talents as a third source user becomes a bit crushed (unless we get some new explanations).<br /> <br /> My vote would go for a option where each of the types is unique branch (or at least no mix and Mach once the gene kick in). a Stalwart is a not fully evolved Nova, not capable yet of the external control over quantum, but enough to powerup himself with no risk of taint. A Mesmerist is a not fully evolved Psiad, not capable of reaching the high levels of power others can, but yet essentially Psi user.<br /> <br /> Yet... they should use a common ground for the 3, as they are not too far from baseline human, as a Talent that can use Biotech and Q-Tech (very limited use), they are so low powered that the quantum used by a Stalwart can still interact with the Psi of a Mesmerist in a non destructive or non repellent way. Basically they are all Inspiration.<br /> <br /> About the powers being variations of Gifts, I doubt, even in 1e Daredevils were the different ones, with one level of Knacks and a different way to deal with it (more about narrative than about real powers). I believe the powers form Stalwarts and Mesmerists will be closer to Superior Powers (and so Edges) than to Gifts (I personally would call Superior Edges and not Superior Powers, much like the Enhanced Edges, Inspired Edges and Nova Edges).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T20:36:02-07:00","id":1339111,"title":"","content":"One more element of my take: the justification. You know how the \u00c6on era started with a noetic Event and the Nova era started with a Quantum Event?, Well, the Hammersmith Event wasn't an undifferentiated Event; it was focused on parachronics. The result is the Inspired: all three kinds of Inspired contain a dose of Talent-like influence. Stalwarts are naturally occurring Superiors with a Talent-like upgrade (i.e., Inspiration and access to Dramatic Editing); mesmerists are \u201cfirst generation\u201d psiads with a Talent-like upgrade (same); and daredevils are Talents with possibly a bit more juice (the aforementioned \u201cimproved Dramatic Editing\u201d? Again, I wouldn't give them improved Dramatic Editing unless stalwarts and mesmerists also get a little something extra each beyond their Gift counterparts). <br /> <br /> Put another way, the Adventure! era is awash in parachronic (Telluric?) energies in the same way that the Nova era got bathed in Quantum energies and the \u00c6on era got drenched in noetic energies, thus putting Talents and Dramatic Editing front and center. <br /> <br /> As for Gifts vs. Edges: it's largely a matter of semantics. In terms of game systems, I envision what I've been calling Psychic and Dynamic Gifts working the same way that Mega-Edges and Superior Powers do, with dot ratings to distinguish different degrees of capability (and without the \u201cladder of abilities\u201d structure that Aptitudes and Modes have in TC:\u00c6). So in terms of how they would work, I don't think we have any disagreement. Our main disagreement, if you will, lies in what they should be called. I like calling them Gifts to emphasis their role as counterparts to the Luck/Aptitude(/Intention?) Gifts of the daredevils (and \u201cpsychic gift\u201d has a lot of precedent in the source material). And it has the advantage that the rules can talk about \u201cGifts\u201d instead of having to talk about \u201cGifts and Psychic/Dynamic Edges\u201d when referring to the special abilities that the Inspired can develop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-02-2019, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T03:40:51-07:00","id":1339153,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know if Hammersmith was focused on Talents. As I see, Talents are the easiest ones to erupt, \u201canything\u201d can erupt them, probably because how close they are from regular people. Bhurano event in 2104 erupted Talents and Psiads, for example, and I would say that the number of Talents also increased after N-day. So I guess they would erupt no matter what kind of source is used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-03T10:13:44-07:00","id":1339211,"title":"","content":"I don't <i>know</i> if it was, either. My post was <i>in the context of my take on how TC:A! should be done</i>, not a declaration of established Canon. <br /> <br /> I'm saying that a Talent-focused event could be used to explain why everyone empowered in the Adventure era has features that in later eras are unique to Talents (i.e., Inspiration and Dramatic Editing); and if you want to give stalwarts and mesmerists a little something extra (as precursors to what their later-era counterparts get), it can also explain why this era's daredevils could have a little something extra, too (despite later-era Talents not getting it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T17:51:26-07:00","id":1341028,"title":"","content":"Do you think the Hammersmith Event was an accident, or do you think it was caused by someone else the way the other two big Events were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T18:45:34-07:00","id":1341032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341028#post1341028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think the Hammersmith Event was an accident, or do you think it was caused by someone else the way the other two big Events were?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as 1e tell us, it was an accident for sure. It was intended to be an engine that run on teluric energy that overflow somehow and exploded. The other experiments were intentional but I don\u2019t know if they caused any direct deaths, and for sure the guys causing it had far more experience than Hammersmith on the workings of the \u201cteluric\u201d energies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 10-12-2019, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T20:19:35-07:00","id":1341043,"title":"","content":"I hope we get new Allegiances this edition<br /> <br /> - La Revolte Eclatante\u2019s history should have them existing in the era<br /> <br /> - masked mystery men would be a appropriate<br /> <br /> - scientists who have had a vision of the future and are dedicated to stopping certain avenues of weapons research","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T04:08:45-07:00","id":1341074,"title":"","content":"I wonder if telluric energy is the same thing as what they call Flux in the new Aeon book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T12:20:48-07:00","id":1341118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341074#post1341074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if telluric energy is the same thing as what they call Flux in the new Aeon book.</div> </div> </div> </div>you mean the Trinity Continuum book? Because as Flux is used in the Aeon book is unambiguously Quantum and counter to Noetic energies that could trigger Mesmerists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T13:58:14-07:00","id":1341130,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Thank you!! I didn\u2019t know that. I guess I got confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:01:31-07:00","id":1341131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341130#post1341130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Thank you!! I didn\u2019t know that. I guess I got confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, the Flux Zones in Aeon are caused by Aberrants using extreme powers, and specifically shrank because of the Noetic wave in 2104. They\u2019re the only places Nova Eruptions still happen for the most part, because the rest of Earth is too Noetic in the Psion age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:02:05-07:00","id":1341132,"title":"","content":"I skimmed the Trinity Continuum preview a long time ago and I only read the last chapter of the Aeon book. I guess I got the two confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:02:40-07:00","id":1341133,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:37:01-07:00","id":1341143,"title":"","content":"Well, the Trinity Continuum core book does use Flux to refer to that thing that empowers Talents; so your point is still valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:45:53-07:00","id":1341146,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> got it! That must have been where I got confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T16:44:23-07:00","id":1341173,"title":"","content":"Flux is one of those things that seems to be multiple things to multiple people. On one hand its what 'powers' Talents. On the other hand it, in its Quantum variant, is what happens when bad energies of a Nova are unleashed. <br /> <br /> As an aside Telluric Energy isn't really its own separate unique thing, it is what one 'sees' when they don't have the ability to perceive the indivdual energies of Quantum, Psi, and that which makes Talents work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T19:01:29-07:00","id":1341194,"title":"","content":"In Aberrant, after the Heal power, they say there are 2 different flux, the first is the one described in Core, and the other (the one that Aberrant talks about, is the Quantum Flux. They are not the same, one is Quantum and the other is trans dimensional/trans temporal energy that power Talents in some kind of way.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I would say a Talent can be \u201cerupted\u201d by quantum flux, as they can hangdog quantum in some way, for example powering Q-Tech, but it\u2019s still different, as they can power Noetic tech too, so... Talent (Core) flux is \u201cteluric\u201d as a mix of energies, while quantum flux is pure quantum (and corruption)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T22:48:26-07:00","id":1341221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341173#post1341173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flux is one of those things that seems to be multiple things to multiple people. On one hand its what 'powers' Talents. On the other hand it, in its Quantum variant, is what happens when bad energies of a Nova are unleashed.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, this is a case of two very different things sharing the same name: what TC calls Flux and what TC:\u00c6 and TC:Ab call Flux are fundamentally different. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341173#post1341173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside Telluric Energy isn't really its own separate unique thing, it is what one 'sees' when they don't have the ability to perceive the indivdual energies of Quantum, Psi, and that which makes Talents work.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's true in 1e. It's too soon to know if that's still true in 2e; it's entirely possible that in 2e, Telluric Energy will be \u201cthat which makes Talents work\u201d (what TC calls Flux), with mesmerists and stalwarts not having Psi or Quantum in the same way that Superiors don't have Quantum but are still Quantum-oriented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T08:56:42-07:00","id":1341266,"title":"","content":"I'm not an expert in this area, but it seems like if an explosion of telluric energy created Mesmerists, Stalwarts and Daredevils, then telluric energy is probably a combination of Psi, Quantum and Flux (the kind of Flux used by Talents).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:31:37-07:00","id":1341286,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea that Telluric Energy was the combination of the three other focused types of energy. That because of this fact it was limited in some ways but more capable of others. <br /> <br /> 1e never supported that conclusion, hence my comments above. But it was how I thought, and still kind of do. <br /> <br /> The other idea I like is the image of Telluric Energy being the shore upon which two (or three) oceans meet. The ocean deeps are where Psi, Quantum, and that which powers Talents reside while where they meet is something unique. <br /> <br /> Obviously we don't know how 2e Adventure! will handle it. That said, one of the things I like about Superiors - which may or may not actually apply to others - is that there is no power currency. You have a power, it works, that is it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:31:25-07:00","id":1341313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341266#post1341266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not an expert in this area, but it seems like if an explosion of telluric energy created Mesmerists, Stalwarts and Daredevils, then telluric energy is probably a combination of Psi, Quantum and Flux (the kind of Flux used by Talents).</div> </div> </div> </div>the conceptual problem I\u2019m having with a Psi Quantum combo is the two energies should cancel each other out the setting physics as we know them at this point. I increasingly like your idea of Telluric Energy/Z-Waves being (TC) Flux, and Mesmerists and Stalwarts rather than being directly triggered by Noetic and Quantum Energies respectively, are evolutionary offshoots of Talents with different Gift sets that are developing the ability to harness the other energy types. The full jump to Novas and Psiads arising instead of Stalwarts and Mesmerists come when humanity makes the leap to fully channeling said energies.<br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t fully account for Michael and Sara though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:40:20-07:00","id":1341314,"title":"","content":"Thanks \ud83d\ude0a (assuming you meant me). And I like the way you fleshed it out. If I ever run TC, I\u2019ll probably use something like that.<br /> <br /> I personally think Michael Donighal, Sara Bhurano (I forget her maiden name) and Max Mercer are basically just extremely powerful examples of novas, psiads and Talents. Does this make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:55:30-07:00","id":1341317,"title":"","content":"Michael and Sarah are the reason I think the \u201cteluric\u201d is a mix, and Hammersmith explosion was a combination of the 3 energies. The impact of the Flux (not Quantum flux), probably is the thing that brought the other dimension shards to the main timeline.<br /> <br /> on 1e it was the combination of Psi and Quantum that did it, but in 2e it seams it\u2019s flux itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:59:31-07:00","id":1341318,"title":"","content":"I've always assumed in the Adventure! era they didn't have as precise of measuring tools. So, Telluric Energy was really just three energies with enough similarity to be confused for each other if viewed through the equivalent of a microscope with vaseline on the lens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T14:00:50-07:00","id":1341319,"title":"","content":"Hmm, so based on the above theory Talents use pure Flux, while Stalwarts use Quantum-influenced Flux and Mesmerists use Psi-influenced Flux. The result is that they all have a similar underlying structure but diverge a bit in how their powers express themselves. (Which also thematically works with the whole idea of 'Michael Donigal has most stalwart gifts and dynamic versions of many psychic gifts.&quot; Yeah, I can dig this. <br /> <br /> It also can explain why Talents could potentially have certain highly specialized gifts that might interact with certain front facing Quantum or Psi powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T14:40:41-07:00","id":1341323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341318#post1341318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed in the Adventure! era they didn't have as precise of measuring tools. So, Telluric Energy was really just three energies with enough similarity to be confused for each other if viewed through the equivalent of a microscope with vaseline on the lens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s definitely the case in 1e. What I\u2019m not sure of though is why the Noetic and Quantum energies wouldn\u2019t have canceled each other out given that that\u2019s an important setting trait they have (its why Eruptions are so rare outside Flux zones in the Aeon era, why the Flux Zones shrank in 2104, why the Quantum barrier around the solar system cracked, why the Doyen are so afraid of Novas and Quantakinesis, etc etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T16:01:43-07:00","id":1341337,"title":"","content":"I think low level quantum and psi don\u2019t nullify each other, only the excess of quantum is dangerous and disturb psi. I mean, there is no psi user in the same level as a Aberrant (Q4+), so we are assuming Psi is more in tune with life, but maybe it\u2019s as dangerous as Quantum in high doses.<br /> <br /> About Psi and Quantum nullifying each other in Adventure, the same could be said about Psiads existing in Nova Era, they would be de powered by the Novas before getting Psi 2, so not discovering their powers. If you think a Quantum Flux Zone as a broken area in space, that quantum is floating out of control and psi requires an stable time-space area to work, than low quantum and even Novas are not really the problem, but the instability caused by the prolonged overuse of the quantum field in the area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T17:40:42-07:00","id":1341352,"title":"","content":"To be explicit:<br /> <br /> &quot;Flux&quot; is the term used for the &quot;fuel&quot; used by Talents. <br /> <br /> &quot;Quantum Flux&quot; is the term for the bad side of Quantum energies in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> The terms share an origin but aren't referring to the same thing, strictly speaking.<br /> <br /> Telluric energy, aka Z-waves, Z-rays, neocaloric fluid, etc etc etc are terms from Adventure!. Inspired researchers recognize that something's happening, but aren't yet sophisticated enough to realize that three different things are happening. Psi, Quantum, and Flux are all conflated as being the same thing. In game terms, Adventure! doesn't distinguish between the three. In metaphyical terms, we, the players, know better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T17:49:52-07:00","id":1341354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341352#post1341352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be explicit:<br /> <br /> &quot;Flux&quot; is the term used for the &quot;fuel&quot; used by Talents.<br /> <br /> &quot;Quantum Flux&quot; is the term for the bad side of Quantum energies in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> The terms share an origin but aren't referring to the same thing, strictly speaking.<br /> <br /> Telluric energy, aka Z-waves, Z-rays, neocaloric fluid, etc etc etc are terms from Adventure!. Inspired researchers recognize that something's happening, but aren't yet sophisticated enough to realize that three different things are happening. Psi, Quantum, and Flux are all conflated as being the same thing. In game terms, Adventure! doesn't distinguish between the three. In metaphyical terms, we, the players, know better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if the presence of Noetic energy diminishing the impact of the Quantum, and vice-versa, is why (with the two exceptions) the Hammersmith event produced Mesmerists and Stalwarts instead of Psiads and Novas.<br /> <br /> Alternatively I can fanwank an explanation about how the blast was Qantum powered in one reality, but Noetic in another, and the Flux combined the two realities allowing both to have their impact without negating each other, as would have happened if you set off Noetic and Quantum explosions at the same time in the same reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:30:05-07:00","id":1341388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341354#post1341354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if the presence of Noetic energy diminishing the impact of the Quantum, and vice-versa, is why (with the two exceptions) the Hammersmith event produced Mesmerists and Stalwarts instead of Psiads and Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although Quantum and Psi are often described as opposites, they're not as wholly opposite as, say, matter and anti-matter. They don't explode on contact. At low enough energy levels, there's some wiggle room for them to operate with each other without conflicting too much.<br /> <br /> You know how the same genetic sequence can express as a nova or psion, depending on how it's flipped? At those lower energy levels, Quantum and Psi behave similarly. Is it a wave-like particle, or a particle-like wave? Yes. So that allows all three Inspired to manifest.<br /> <br /> Something like the blast from the Aberrant Era was higher-energy in the Quantum end of things, and as a result, that inhibited (but didn't entirely prevent) the proliferation of Psi and psiads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively I can fanwank an explanation about how the blast was Qantum powered in one reality, but Noetic in another, and the Flux combined the two realities allowing both to have their impact without negating each other, as would have happened if you set off Noetic and Quantum explosions at the same time in the same reality. </div> </div> </div>Oo, that's kind of clever. Not the direction we're going, but I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T21:10:58-07:00","id":1341395,"title":"","content":"That explanation could be used for a fourth event that's like the first in that it leads to a proliferation of all three types, but does so at a higher power level. <br /> <br /> But that's not TC:A!.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T06:35:33-07:00","id":1341430,"title":"","content":"Maybe high levels of Flux (Talent power) buffer Quantum and Noetic power from each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T07:25:56-07:00","id":1341436,"title":"","content":"I don't think they Ban each other, as Ian said, they are not opposed to each other, so its possible to power both with a single event (as Hammersmith).<br /> <br /> As I said, I think the problem is the corruption excess quantum can cause on the environment and creatures, making everything unstable, including the Noetic field. So Stalwarts and Superiors can use psi related super science, they still have a Psi value, etc.<br /> <br /> What happen on Nova Era is, what ever Mal did increased the chance of eruption to FAR above any natural level, and also increased the natural level of eruption to a Nova level. The presence of Novas can erupt new novas (they say that somewhere in Aberrant 1e, can't remember the book, but I read it a few weeks ago), it is also one of the possible eruption causes (exposition to Quantum powers) in 1e, so the excess of novas cause more novas to erupt.<br /> <br /> Regular level Quantum users (not sure if a Stalwart or something in between a Nova and a Stalwart, like a Psiad to a Mesmerist) would be more balanced, like Psiads are, and would not cause more eruptions by simple power use (as happen to Psiads and Psions).<br /> <br /> The quantum flux zones are places where there is a high amount of quantum instability, the same effect or even higher than the presence of other Novas, what would cause a increased chance of natural eruption of novas, or sub aberrants in the caso of people that would not be capable of erupt properly.<br /> <br /> TL/DR : It's not the number of psions that block novas to erupt, it's the lack of a high quantum instability that do that (in opposition to Nova Era and Quantum Flux Zones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T02:15:05-07:00","id":1341600,"title":"","content":"How about the chances of Nova eruption on Eden?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2893-muon","name":"muon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T02:52:19-07:00","id":1341606,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s one of the points that indicate Novas erupt because of novas, they are erupting in Eden just because there are Novas there, small number than the Earth, but also the total population of the world is pretty small.<br /> <br /> There could be a Psiad in the middle, but they are so rare that even 1 in a million is too much, so probably no Psiads (maybe 1).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:03:57-07:00","id":1341656,"title":"","content":"Well the fact that Edenites consider Psions to be just like Novas on a social standing level could easily mean that if they did have a Psiad said Psiad would be treated in the exact same way as the Novas. <br /> <br /> Imagine a Psiad on Eden with QK due to being around so many Novas. That could be interesting. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:44:26-07:00","id":1341685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1341600#post1341600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about the chances of Nova eruption on Eden?</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly like the odds of one erupting on Earth in 2028, maybe a bit higher, but you do hit a ceiling because only a subset of the population has the potential to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-16-2019, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T04:22:09-07:00","id":1342915,"title":"","content":"Adventure! in on Draft! That\u2019s good and made me happy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T05:49:23-07:00","id":1342925,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz awesome!! Adventure! is my favorite of the three Trinity games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T06:19:24-07:00","id":1342929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1339029-adventure-2e?p=1342925#post1342925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz awesome!! Adventure! is my favorite of the three Trinity games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree! Back in the old Nexus forums, we were putting together splats for Adventure. Mostly surrounding WW2 adventures and using Adventure themes in different settings. Popular ones were &quot;retro&quot; now settings like Gotham/Dark Night type worlds and alternate histories like Sky Captain and the World of Tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T06:52:46-07:00","id":1342933,"title":"","content":"I like pulp stuff with a lot of noir and a little postmodernism thrown in. I like the character of Annabelle Newfield and how Michael Donighal looked after her like a daughter, to the point that he quit the Aeon Society out of grief when she died. I might end up playing a character sort of like her when we finally get around to playing Adventure!. Except without the chewing tobacco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T07:46:42-07:00","id":1342943,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m really hopeful that the developers stick with something similar to the Superior template for Stalwarts, but scaled up enough to handle Hugo Danner at the very top end. Maybe make use of some of the scale rules the way Aberrant has, without being quite so free form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T08:41:48-07:00","id":1342950,"title":"","content":"My favourite is Adventure! not much because of the pulp part, of course the pulp is great, but the feeling of the game, the level of power, the flexibility for characters and ways to play. You can have a metaplot game, with Aeon society as the center of the game, or you can explore all the rest of the world, the different societies and the \u201cTerra Incognitae\u201d.<br /> <br /> Than, there is the rule set, I love the way it work, it\u2019s less flexible than Aberrant in terms of powers, but the way It works and how you can build a variety of characters is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T11:08:35-07:00","id":1342974,"title":"","content":"Adventure! is funny in that the setting for me is okay but the rules, mechanics, and powers of the three Inspired are things I absolutely love. Inspired Knacks (or Gifts if we use core book naming) is structured in a way I love, especially with the developments we see present in both Talents and Superiors. They are capable, powerful, but lower then say super Nova powers so as to not be world breaking when applied to a setting. The fact that various character types and such can be built using the rules also is fun. I also really like the fact hat as all three types use (at least in 1e) the same general rules framework one can take from each to build a character that logically does what you need them to do. (This was seen in Michael Donigal who has all Stalwart knacks and also stalwart versions of heroic and psychic knacks. Simple, effective, awesome.) <br /> <br /> So yeah, I am eagerly looking forward to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:06:26-07:00","id":1342992,"title":"","content":"Very eager to see how the pulp elements of the Adventure! game will be re-imagined for The Trinity Continuum <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> that the powers of all three Inspired in one place and time was amazing and I can't wait to see it again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}